title the repair that came home
prompt adopt 6420adc891's caravan repair onto xy
think Adoption across a rewrite is file-wise, never a merge -- %290's own lesson, learned when a worktree merged across a history rewrite and silently resolved LEXICON.md to a rewritten historical blob. And the reach is git checkout <ref> -- <path>, never git show <ref>:<path> > <path>, because %294 proved this morning in a pen that a blob carries no mode while the tree object does. Both disciplines were written by this tree in the last twelve hours and both applied here in the first minute.
think Before adopting anything I asked whether the repair was still wanted, since an adoption that fixes nothing is worse than none. Two faults, both live. The suite's roster check runs find tools -maxdepth 2 -name 'caravan_*_witness.rish', and exactly eight tools/ca files carried no _witness suffix -- so eight witnesses stood outside the bijection the suite exists to prove. And the SIGTERM witness carried only the Sound pier's weaker exec repair, which fixes which pid is named and still returns over a live supervisor on the timeout path.
think Then whether adopting would cost anything. Every file the commit modifies was byte-identical to the fork parent in this tree, checked by comparing blob hashes rather than by reading diffs, so a wholesale checkout reverts no upstream work. That check is what made the adoption a checkout rather than a patch, and it is the check I would have skipped if I had trusted the shape of the story.
think The citations were the part that needed judgment. The adopted files cite REDS %289 four times, and %289 in this tree is an unrelated sed-tamper red -- the very collision the shelf's own header describes happening to it once already. Repointed those four to %297 and left the fifth alone, since caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish's %289 is pre-existing and correct. A blanket sed would have broken a true citation to fix four false ones.
think One defect in the adopted work itself: tools/fixtures/caravan_subscribe_poll_signal.sh opens by naming the witness it serves, and it named the pre-rename spelling. The commit renamed the witness and left its own fixture's first line pointing at the old name. Fixed on arrival rather than adopted as written.
think The row re-seated a third time. Booked %289 on the pre-rewrite lineage, re-seated %290 there, and now %297 here, because %290 through %296 are all spoken for. That is the sixth firing of the row-number door and the shelf now says so in its own header. The pattern is no longer an accident of timing: a row number is allocated by whoever pushes first, three stars push into one tree, and the derived-spine key that would end it has been waiting at Keaton's door through all six.
obs Proven rather than asserted. caravan_subscribe_poll_signal_witness.rish runs GREEN on this pier, the roster bijection reads 121 on disk and 121 registered where eight were invisible before, and four of the renamed witnesses were run individually and are GREEN. The card's RED line is retired because the witness passes here, not because the diff looked right.
obs The session log came across as dated testimony and keeps every number it wrote, including the %289 and %290 that mean something else here. A stale reference is resolved rather than rewritten, so the shelf header and the recital carry the resolution and the log keeps its word.
